---
// Running a model by hand, without the router: the resolver and the routing
// table, computed by the kit at build time. Machinery, under the docs.
import DocLayout from '../../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import LaneResolver from '../../components/LaneResolver.astro';
import RoutingTable from '../../components/RoutingTable.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import kit from '../../data/kit.json';
import table from '../../data/routing-table.json';

// The legend only earns its place when some role is unsupported.
const anyUnsupported = table.profiles.some((row) => !row.technical_compatibility);
---

<DocLayout
  title="Run a model by hand — delegation-kit"
  description="Without the router: send one task to one model you name, from Claude Code or Codex, and get a receipt."
  path="/docs/dispatch"
>
  <h1>Run a model by hand</h1>

  <p>
    You pick a profile and a role (the kind of job, such as builder or reviewer; the CLI flag is
    <code>--lane</code>). It runs once, within its adapter's limits, and writes a receipt. Claude Code
    and Codex do this only when you ask, and a retry or a review is a new run you ask for.
  </p>
  <div class="not-prose">
    <CodeBlock
      label="Terminal"
      code={`delegation-route resolve --lane builder --json        # lists, runs nothing
delegation-route resolve --lane builder --selected-profile ID --json   # validates only
delegation-run --profile ID --lane builder \\
  --prompt-file task.md --output result.txt --workdir WORKTREE`}
    />
  </div>
  <p>
    A run writes the output and a <code>.result.json</code> receipt; a failure writes
    <code>.error.json</code> and exits with a <a href="/docs/executors/#exit-codes">code</a>. Fields and
    flags: <a href="/docs/configuration/#selection-and-execution">Configuration</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Let the decider propose one</h2>
  <p>
    With a router block, the decider rates the task, keeps the pool profiles that take the role and that
    this machine can reach, and recommends the cheapest one strong enough, with its reasons. It runs
    nothing: you run PROFILE, or ask Claude Code or Codex to. Rules:
    <a href="/docs/router/">Router</a>.
  </p>
  <div class="not-prose">
    <CodeBlock
      label="Terminal"
      code={`delegation-router decide --prompt-file task.md --lane builder --json
delegation-run --profile PROFILE --lane builder \\
  --prompt-file task.md --output result.txt --workdir WORKTREE`}
    />
  </div>
  <p>
    In the v5 catalog, Terra/high scores 42.3, Sol/max 54.5 and Opus/max 58.4.
    A rating of 2 requires 38.4; a rating of 3 requires 50.4. The router compares
    estimated token prices only among profiles whose measured effort clears the minimum.

  </p>

  <h2>Which profiles can take a role</h2>
  <p>Pick a role. Computed from kit {kit.version} when the site was built.</p>
  <div class="not-prose">
    <LaneResolver />
  </div>

  <h2>Every role, every profile</h2>
  <p>{kit.profiles} profiles from the default install.</p>
  <div class="not-prose">
    {
      anyUnsupported && (
        <p class="text-[0.75rem] mb-4">
          <span class="status status-unsupported">unsupported</span> the adapter does not support this role;
          never selectable
        </p>
      )
    }
    <RoutingTable />
  </div>

  <p>
    What each adapter may touch, how its model is checked, and how <code>delegation-patch-verify</code>
    checks a text model's patch before you apply it: <a href="/docs/executors/">Executors</a>.
  </p>
</DocLayout>
